Package: spatialHMRF
Title: Spatial Domains with a Hidden Markov Random Field
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Qian", "Zhu", role = "aut",
        comment = "original HMRF method and smfishHmrf implementation"),
    person("Guo-Cheng", "Yuan", email = "guo-cheng.yuan@mssm.edu",
        role = "aut"),
    person("Ruben", "Dries", email = "rubendries@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7650-7754"))
    )
Description: Finds spatial domains by fitting the hidden Markov random field
    (HMRF) model of Zhu et al. (2018) <doi:10.1038/nbt.4260>: each cell's
    z-scored expression of spatial genes follows a multivariate Gaussian per
    domain, and a Potts prior favours domains shared with spatial neighbours.
    The model is fitted by expectation-maximization with iterated conditional
    modes over the colour classes of the spatial network, from a k-means
    start, as in the 'smfishHmrf' package. Colour classes are independent
    sets, so each update is a sparse matrix product; results equal
    'smfishHmrf' on the same inputs.
